<title>FRANCE: ISIS buys stakes from Elf Aquitaine.</title>
<headline>ISIS buys stakes from Elf Aquitaine.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Internationale de Services Industriels et Scientifiques (ISIS) said it had bought a 10 percent stake in Geophysique from oil group Elf Aquitaine, taking its stake to 19.9 percent.</p>
<p>It also bought a 3.6 percent stake in Coflexip Stena Offshore from Sogelfa, an Elf company, bring its stake in this company also to 19.9 percent.</p>
<p>ISIS did not give financial details.  </p>
<p>ISIS is 57 percent owned by the Institut Francais du Petrole, 39 percent by Elf and four percent by bank BNP.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
